 {"id":"fabro-8ee1","title":"Engine: fabro_run_create must structurally reject a duplicate develop child while a sibling of the same parent is non-terminal (conductor recreated a child after wait-timeout)","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-10T14:53:25.284Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-10T15:25:20.506Z","description":"WHAT HAPPENED (2026-09-10 14:31-14:48 UTC): conductor 01M25R5K62JQWZR0YV8HC88BEQ's develop leg created child #1 (01M25R832HP6, fabro-3fe4) at 13:31. The leg's `fabro_run_wait {until: terminal, timeout_ms: 3600000}` hit its 60-minute budget at 14:31:25 (the seed legitimately needed ~80 min). Instead of re-waiting the EXISTING child (prompt: 'reached=timeout (child still running): call again ... NEVER create a second child'), the agent called `fabro_run_create` at 14:34:23 and produced child #2 (01M25VVK131J, claimed fabro-7627). Child #2 was cancelled at 14:44:03 (user cleanup), the leg routed 'Develop child failed', and the pass failed — leaving child #1 orphaned but still running. CLASS: second live instance of the recreate-after-failure documented for 2026-09-05 (approval_required -> recreate); prompt rules are advisory and the documented case plus this one show the model violates them exactly under time pressure. DURABLE FIX (engine-side, structural serialization instead of prompt prose): `fabro_run_create` rejects (or requires an explicit override flag on) creating a child of the same parent+workflow kind while another child of that parent is non-terminal — the caller gets an error naming the existing child id and is structurally forced to re-wait. Secondary knob (prompt, cheap): raise the develop leg's terminal-wait budget above the longest expected seed duration (80+ min observed) or make re-wait-after-timeout the only legal continuation with the create tool unavailable mid-leg. Basis: runs 01M25R5K62JQWZR0YV8HC88BEQ (conductor), 01M25R832HP615J291N72FHNCS (child #1, orphaned), 01M25VVK131JTQB3BRBPAV0DWR (child #2, cancelled), 2026-09-10\n\nFIX IMPLEMENTED 2026-09-10 15:2x (line paused, direct agent repair, pending PR): lib/components/fabro-tool/src/create.rs reject_duplicate_active_child() — fabro_run_create rejects a same-workflow child while a sibling is non-terminal, error names the existing child id (message carries fabro-8ee1); terminal siblings and different-workflow siblings stay allowed. 3 new tests. Develop-leg prompt updated: timeout => re-wait the SAME child, never recreate. Basis addition: commit pending on denkhaus.","labels":["engine","workflows"],"assignee":"fabro"}
